<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen Apr cotton fibre output down 76 pct on Mar.</title>
<headline>Turkmen Apr cotton fibre output down 76 pct on Mar.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's production of cotton fibre fell by 76 percent in April from March, to 600 tonnes, a report from the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    TURKMEN COTTON FIBRE OUTPUT  Apr '97   Mar '97   Jan-Apr '97</p>
<p>    Cotton fibre (thousand tonnes)  0.6	2.5	  22.4</p>
<p>    Month-on-month pct change     -76.0    -55.4	   n/a</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	   n/a	n/a	 -79.4</p>
<p>The committee, which provided no data for exports, said 91 percent of cotton fibre was sold to Hong Kong, Pakistan, Switzerland, Britain, Sweden, Austria and Bulgaria.</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
